{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -euo pipefail\nSKILL=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260810T205301Z-pilot-142-final/1.4.1/worker/planning\nPLAN_DIR=.plans/basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T205301Z-pilot-142-final-isolated-plan\nu(){ \"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" \"$@\"; }\nu --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-contract/01-step-root-markup instructions -p 5.1: \"Create button-chain.html as a standalone document. In the #button-chain-root subtree, render exactly one initial button at load, give it a stable accessible name, and do not render finished text or hidden extra buttons.\"\nu --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-contract/01-step-root-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"A reviewer can inspect the future file and identify one initial button inside #button-chain-root, no other button elements, and no completion message in the initial state.\"\nu --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-contract/01-step-root-markup handoff -p 7.1: \"W02 can attach behavior to the initial button and any generated current-last button without changing the root markup target.\"\nu --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-contract/02-step-append-handler instructions -p 5.1: \"Implement appendNextButton() in button-chain.html. It must respond only when the clicked element is the current last button, increment the generated-button count by one, create exactly one new button, and insert that new button below the clicked last button.\"\nu --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-contract/02-step-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"After each nonterminal last-button click, the number of visible buttons increases by exactly one, the new button appears below the prior last button, and clicking an older non-last button cannot append another button.\"\nu --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-contract/02-step-append-handler handoff -p 7.1: \"W03 can use the same generated-butt